WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.137 --> 00:00:03.427
Proposition forty-one combines audits with changes to state

2
00:00:03.427 --> 00:00:04.727
spending-limit rules.

3
00:00:05.013 --> 00:00:07.813
The measure concerns new or increased state special

4
00:00:07.813 --> 00:00:08.213
taxes.

5
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.980
The initial audit must identify ways to reduce

6
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.840
annual program costs by ten percent.

7
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.440
Identifying options is not the same as delivering

8
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:20.240
savings or proving that services can stay unchanged.

9
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.180
Prop forty-one could block Prop forty if both

10
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.200
pass and forty-one receives more yes votes, subject

11
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.660
to how courts interpret their conflict.

12
00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:32.307
A voter might want evidence of efficiency before

13
00:00:32.307 --> 00:00:36.267
approving new dedicated taxes, and regular follow-up

14
00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:36.607
afterward.

15
00:00:36.907 --> 00:00:40.067
Another voter could favor oversight but object to

16
00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:44.107
mandatory reviews of measures that never qualify, or

17
00:00:44.107 --> 00:00:46.087
to limits on funding flexibility.

18
00:00:46.727 --> 00:00:49.447
Yes adds audits and spending-limit provisions;

19
00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:51.847
no keeps the current framework.

20
00:00:52.147 --> 00:00:53.827
Visit our website for the fuller explanation,

21
00:00:54.647 --> 00:00:56.607
source links, and official voter guide.
